; equality_grows_past_the_index_width: an index of i64::MAX is charged as a
; growth, not clamped away, so the fault is the budget's and not the target's.
;
; EQUALITY grows the model to cover the largest index it was handed, and the
; needed size is that index plus one. At i64::MAX that addition overflows the
; charge width. Clamping the overflow to zero would charge nothing, pass
; the size range check on a size of zero and fall through to
; IndexOutOfBounds, at the 1 GiB default budget this vector runs at.
;
; The overflow clamps up instead, to i64::MAX. The exact needed size would
; be 2^63, one variable more, but the charge cannot see the difference: both
; cost more than four times a u64 and are refused for that reason rather
; than by comparison against any particular budget. MemoryLimitExceeded is
; therefore the answer at every budget a host can express, which is what
; this vector pins.

PUSH 1
BQMX r0
VECI r1
VECI r2
PUSH 9223372036854775807
VECPUSH r1
PUSH 1
VECPUSH r2
PUSH 1
PUSH 1
EQUALITY r0 r1 r2
HALT
